+## Changed
+
+- Deleted `src/cli/done.ts` and `src/core/lifecycle/done.ts`.
+- `src/cli/index.ts`: removed the `doneCommand` import and the
+  `done <id> <task>` command registration. No other change.
+- Deleted `tests/done-manual.test.ts`.
+- `tests/command-error-changes.test.ts`: removed the two `done throws` cases
+  and nothing else.
+- `tests/worktree-lifecycle.test.ts`: removed the
+  `manual done writes the marker in the worktree` case and the
+  `markTaskDoneManual` import; nothing else.
+- Added `tests/done-removed.test.ts`: `createProgram()` registers no `done`
+  command, `done 001 1 --manual x` through `createProgram` in a temp project
+  with change `001` exits non-zero and writes no `.run/done/1`, and the two
+  done command source files do not exist.
+- Left the typed `done_manual` event, the `[manual]` outcome line, the report
+  manual counts, and doctor's done-markers check untouched.
+
+## Deviated
+
+- `tests/done-removed.test.ts` uses a local capture helper rather than
+  `tests/cli-capture.ts`. An unknown command makes Commander call
+  `process.exit` directly; `runCliCaptured` stubs `process.exit` to throw and
+  then rethrows, so it cannot report the exit code. The local helper stubs
+  `process.exit` the same way but treats that throw as the captured exit,
+  which is what the acceptance line asks it to observe.
+
+Touched: src/cli/index.ts, src/cli/done.ts, src/core/lifecycle/done.ts, tests/done-manual.test.ts, tests/command-error-changes.test.ts, tests/worktree-lifecycle.test.ts, tests/done-removed.test.ts
